WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.833
Real questions often have more than one part.

2
00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:09.141
In this lesson, you will learn to filter with several conditions at once, such

3
00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:14.449
as gender, province and marital status together, and you will learn what it means

4
00:00:14.449 --> 00:00:16.724
when a filter returns no rows.

5
00:00:16.724 --> 00:00:18.620
Let's dig a little deeper.

6
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:25.440
Under the note, complex filter, I start a new table called Deep Filter.

7
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.072
Demographic, pipe, filter. The first condition:

8
00:00:38.072 --> 00:00:40.120
Gender, double equals, Male.

9
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.910
Then a comma, and the second condition:

10
00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.572
Province, double equals, Badakhshan.

11
00:00:56.572 --> 00:00:59.482
In a filter, a comma means and.

12
00:00:59.482 --> 00:01:01.560
Every condition must be true.

13
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.788
A third condition on a new line:

14
00:01:14.788 --> 00:01:16.780
Marital Status, double equals, Single.

15
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.649
Run it, and look at the Environment:

16
00:01:37.649 --> 00:01:39.162
Deep Filter, zero observations.

17
00:01:39.162 --> 00:01:41.054
Is that an error? No!

18
00:01:41.054 --> 00:01:42.568
It is an answer.

19
00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:49.000
In this data, there is no row that matches all three conditions as I first typed them.

20
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.403
Let's change one condition, from Single to Married, and run it again.

21
00:01:59.403 --> 00:02:01.604
Now we get a different result.

22
00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:06.740
Changing one condition at a time is a great way to explore your data.

23
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.923
And here, with Single, three rows match:

24
00:02:14.923 --> 00:02:17.010
three single men in Badakhshan.

25
00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.680
View shows them clearly.

26
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.614
Notice how each condition narrows the table a little more. First, all men.

27
00:02:45.614 --> 00:02:47.341
Then, men in Badakhshan.

28
00:02:47.341 --> 00:02:49.500
Then, single men in Badakhshan.

29
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.600
Next, I add a new note:

30
00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.767
converting numerical values to numeric.

31
00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:17.100
We will learn about converting data types soon. Excellent work!

